And so I think Jim kind of feels like, I don't know what I'm supposed to do here.
所以我认为吉姆当时感觉，我不知道自己在这里该做什么。

1288
00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:42.900
I don't know where I fit in anymore.
我不知道自己还能不能融入其中。

1289
00:48:43.240 --> 00:48:43.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1290
00:48:43.620 --> 00:48:44.780
And she's getting married.
而且她快要结婚了。

1291
00:48:45.080 --> 00:48:45.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1292
00:48:45.500 --> 00:48:45.600
Yeah.
没错。

1293
00:48:46.940 --> 00:48:49.560
Then a giant teddy bear arrives.
然后一只巨大的泰迪熊送到了。

1294
00:48:50.620 --> 00:48:54.280
And it's being delivered by two guys in Vance Refrigeration Outfits.
是由两个穿着万斯制冷公司制服的人送来的。

1295
00:48:54.280 --> 00:48:59.360
They were played by our writing team of Gene Stepnitsky and Lee Eisenberg.
他们是由我们的编剧团队成员吉恩·斯泰普尼茨基和李·艾森伯格扮演的。

1296
00:48:59.480 --> 00:49:00.880
But you only see Gene.
但你只能看到吉恩。

1297
00:49:01.100 --> 00:49:02.300
Lee got cut out.
李的戏份被剪掉了。

1298
00:49:02.460 --> 00:49:03.380
Lee got cut out.
李被剪掉了。

1299
00:49:03.520 --> 00:49:04.720
It's in the deleted scene.
在删减片段里有。

1300
00:49:04.720 --> 00:49:05.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1301
00:49:05.140 --> 00:49:06.160
They get in a fist fight.
他们打了一架。

1302
00:49:06.380 --> 00:49:06.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1303
00:49:06.680 --> 00:49:07.620
It's kind of ridiculous.
这有点荒谬。

1304
00:49:08.440 --> 00:49:11.580
But Gene is the person who says, Phyllis Lappin?
但吉恩就是那个说“菲利斯·拉平？”的人。

1305
00:49:12.700 --> 00:49:17.460
So if you're wondering which one is Gene and which one is Lee, Gene is in this episode.
所以如果你在想哪个是吉恩，哪个是李，吉恩就在这一集里。

1306
00:49:17.660 --> 00:49:18.560
And they come back later.
他们之后还会回来。

1307
00:49:18.640 --> 00:49:20.620
They're going to recur and you'll actually get to see Lee.
他们会再次出现，你到时候就能见到李了。

1308
00:49:20.800 --> 00:49:27.660
There's a very funny little sort of exchange between Gene and Brian as Kevin where Kevin's
吉恩和饰演凯文的布莱恩之间有一段非常有趣的对话，凯文当时说，

1309
00:49:27.660 --> 00:49:28.960
like, that thing's as big as me.
那东西跟我一样大。

1310
00:49:29.180 --> 00:49:30.320
And Gene's like, no, it's not.
吉恩说，不，它没有。

1311
00:49:30.420 --> 00:49:30.880
No, it's not.
不，它没有。

1312
00:49:30.960 --> 00:49:31.840
Kevin's like, zip it.
凯文说，闭嘴。

1313
00:49:31.840 --> 00:49:34.780
So now Michael has finally made it to his meeting.
现在迈克尔终于赶到他的会议了。

1314
00:49:35.020 --> 00:49:36.980
He's done wandering the streets of New York.
他不用再在纽约街头游荡了。

1315
00:49:37.420 --> 00:49:41.400
And he's going to meet with the other branch managers in a conference room.
他要去会议室和其他分部经理见面。

1316
00:49:41.900 --> 00:49:48.700
And I just want to mention, we said this earlier, this part of it was not shot in New York.
我只想提一下，我们之前说过，这部分并不是在纽约拍摄的。

1317
00:49:48.860 --> 00:49:50.480
This was shot on some stages.
这是在摄影棚里拍的。

1318
00:49:50.740 --> 00:49:53.400
Right there where we film every day in California.
就在我们每天在加州拍摄的地方。

1319
00:49:53.660 --> 00:49:53.960
Yes.
没错。

1320
00:49:54.580 --> 00:49:55.820
Look out the window.
看看窗外。

1321
00:49:56.140 --> 00:49:57.700
They did such a good job.
他们做得真好。

1322
00:49:57.700 --> 00:50:01.700
The backdrop, it really looks like they're up high in a building in New York.
背景看起来真的很像是在纽约高层建筑里。

1323
00:50:01.840 --> 00:50:04.420
No, they're, the trickery is so good.
不，他们，这障眼法太高明了。

1324
00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:06.220
Our set design team was phenomenal.
我们的布景设计团队太棒了。

1325
00:50:06.480 --> 00:50:06.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1326
00:50:06.780 --> 00:50:09.960
But really, they are on ground level in a warehouse.
但实际上，他们是在仓库的地面层。

1327
00:50:10.160 --> 00:50:11.340
In Van Nuys, California.
在加州的范奈斯。

1328
00:50:11.640 --> 00:50:11.780
Yeah.
没错。

1329
00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:12.540
Kind of amazing.
真是太神奇了。

1330
00:50:12.760 --> 00:50:15.000
But let's meet the other managers.
但让我们来认识一下其他经理吧。

1331
00:50:15.440 --> 00:50:16.720
Yes, I have a card.
好的，我有张名片。

1332
00:50:16.880 --> 00:50:17.160
All right.
好吧。

1333
00:50:17.280 --> 00:50:18.280
Give me your card, lady.
把你的名片给我，女士。

1334
00:50:18.420 --> 00:50:19.400
Here's my card.
这是我的名片。

1335
00:50:19.400 --> 00:50:26.420
So, the other managers are Dan Gore, who manages Buffalo, played by Dan Cole.
那么，其他经理分别是管理布法罗分部的丹·戈尔，由丹·科尔饰演。

1336
00:50:26.740 --> 00:50:29.700
Josh Porter, he manages Stamford Branch.
乔什·波特，他管理斯坦福分部。

1337
00:50:29.940 --> 00:50:33.660
Craig, Michael calls him Craigers, played by Craig Anton, manages Albany.
克雷格，迈克尔叫他“克雷格斯”，由克雷格·安东饰演，管理奥尔巴尼分部。

1338
00:50:33.920 --> 00:50:34.380
Yes.
是的。

1339
00:50:34.600 --> 00:50:37.700
So, here's a little tidbit about the Dan Gore character.
关于丹·戈尔这个角色，有个小花絮。

1340
00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:38.280
Okay.
好的。

1341
00:50:38.600 --> 00:50:45.340
In the DVD commentary, Mike Schur says, the quiet guy in the conference room, he named after his good friend, Dan Gore.
在DVD评论音轨里，迈克·舒尔说，会议室里那个安静的家伙，是以他的好友丹·戈尔的名字命名的。

1342
00:50:45.520 --> 00:50:46.560
The writer, Dan Gore.
就是编剧丹·戈尔。

1343
00:50:46.660 --> 00:50:47.160
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1344
00:50:47.160 --> 00:50:50.100
Dan Gore, who, I mean, he created Brooklyn Nine-Nine.
丹·戈尔，我的意思是，他创作了《神烦警探》。

1345
00:50:50.240 --> 00:50:51.900
He's a phenomenal writer.
他是一位了不起的编剧。

1346
00:50:52.140 --> 00:50:52.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1347
00:50:52.540 --> 00:50:53.940
And he was a friend of Mike's.
他是迈克的朋友。

1348
00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:56.360
And Mindy sort of chimed in that Mike loved to do that.
敏迪也插话说迈克很喜欢那样做。

1349
00:50:56.480 --> 00:50:58.760
He loved to put his friends' names in things.
他喜欢把朋友的名字放进作品里。

1350
00:50:59.220 --> 00:51:00.400
He was a Conan writer.
他曾是《柯南秀》的编剧。

1351
00:51:00.400 --> 00:51:01.620
He wrote on Parks and Rec.
他还参与过《公园与游憩》的编剧工作。

1352
00:51:01.740 --> 00:51:04.560
And now, of course, he's the showrunner of Brooklyn Nine-Nine.
现在，他当然已经是《神烦警探》的剧集主管了。

1353
00:51:04.760 --> 00:51:07.660
So, Dan Gore got a nice little shout out in this episode.
所以，丹·戈尔在这一集中得到了一个小小的致敬。

1354
00:51:07.880 --> 00:51:08.200
Yes.
没错。

1355
00:51:08.380 --> 00:51:10.300
So, we are meeting all the Branch Heads.
所以，我们要见见所有的分部主管了。

1356
00:51:10.840 --> 00:51:12.200
And Craigers is an idiot.
而克雷格是个白痴。

1357
00:51:12.420 --> 00:51:13.120
He's, right?
他是，对吧？

1358
00:51:13.300 --> 00:51:15.880
He's gotten kicked out of all the strip clubs in Albany.
他被奥尔巴尼所有的脱衣舞俱乐部赶出来了。

1359
00:51:16.060 --> 00:51:16.840
Very proud of that.
对此他引以为傲。

1360
00:51:16.840 --> 00:51:17.280
Find out.
去查查看。

1361
00:51:17.420 --> 00:51:19.260
And then he starts insulting Jan.
然后他开始侮辱简。

1362
00:51:19.520 --> 00:51:19.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1363
00:51:20.240 --> 00:51:20.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1364
00:51:20.680 --> 00:51:21.380
He says.
他是这么说的。

1365
00:51:21.660 --> 00:51:23.220
He calls her the B word.
他骂她是那个B开头的词。

1366
00:51:23.220 --> 00:51:23.820
He does.
他确实骂了。

1367
00:51:23.880 --> 00:51:25.680
And Michael comes to her defense.
然后迈克尔站出来维护她。

1368
00:51:25.800 --> 00:51:26.820
He says, oh, come on now.
他说，噢，得了吧。

1369
00:51:26.920 --> 00:51:27.340
Come on now.
得了吧。

1370
00:51:27.520 --> 00:51:31.020
And he stands up for her first by saying, that's my girlfriend.
他先是说“那是我的女朋友”，以此来维护她。

1371
00:51:31.320 --> 00:51:31.660
Oh.
噢。

1372
00:51:31.940 --> 00:51:32.240
Boy.
天哪。

1373
00:51:32.460 --> 00:51:34.840
And then he backpedals and says, I mean, we hooked up.
然后他又改口说，我是说，我们有过一腿。

1374
00:51:35.020 --> 00:51:37.720
And then Josh Porter's like, you hooked up with Jan?
接着乔什·波特就说，你和简有过一腿？

1375
00:51:38.600 --> 00:51:39.980
And now he's in it.
现在他麻烦大了。

1376
00:51:40.100 --> 00:51:41.160
He spilled the beans.
他把秘密泄露了。

1377
00:51:41.340 --> 00:51:42.140
Dang it, Michael.
该死，迈克尔。

1378
00:51:46.840 --> 00:51:50.300
He's talking to people for five minutes and he's already told everyone that he's hooked
他才跟人聊了五分钟，就已经告诉所有人他跟简

1379
00:51:50.300 --> 00:51:50.920
up with Jan.
有过一腿了。

1380
00:51:51.120 --> 00:51:51.900
With their boss.
跟他们的老板。

1381
00:51:52.100 --> 00:51:52.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1382
00:51:52.520 --> 00:51:53.140
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

1383
00:51:53.420 --> 00:51:55.140
And then it's like crickets in the room.
然后房间里一片死寂。

1384
00:51:55.500 --> 00:51:55.860
All right.
好吧。

1385
00:51:55.920 --> 00:51:57.440
Well, maybe we should take a break.
也许我们该休息一下了。

1386
00:51:57.640 --> 00:51:58.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1387
00:51:58.060 --> 00:51:59.320
With that news.
带着这个消息。

1388
00:51:59.320 --> 00:52:03.320
On that news, Michael has just spilled the beans and we'll be right back.
带着这个消息，迈克尔刚刚泄露了秘密，我们马上回来。

1389
00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:03.860
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

1390
00:52:03.860 --> 00:52:07.960
Because one of my favorite scenes is happening back at the office.
因为我最喜欢的场景之一马上要在办公室上演了。

1391
00:52:08.180 --> 00:52:08.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1392
00:52:08.480 --> 00:52:09.400
We need to talk about it.
我们需要聊聊那个场景。

1393
00:52:09.440 --> 00:52:09.860
It's good stuff.
那段很棒。

1394
00:52:10.000 --> 00:52:10.380
It's good.
真的很棒。

1395
00:52:19.100 --> 00:52:19.540
Okay.
好的。

1396
00:52:19.560 --> 00:52:20.240
So we're back.
我们回来了。

1397
00:52:20.380 --> 00:52:25.640
You guys, I have to talk about this scene between Dwight and Pam in the break room.
伙计们，我必须聊聊休息室里德怀特和帕姆的那场戏。

1398
00:52:25.800 --> 00:52:25.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1399
00:52:26.040 --> 00:52:28.300
I loved it so much, Jenna.
我太喜欢那场戏了，珍娜。

1400
00:52:28.540 --> 00:52:30.500
I rewound and watched it a few times.
我倒回去看了好几遍。

1401
00:52:31.640 --> 00:52:32.580
Oh, gosh.
噢，天哪。

1402
00:52:32.740 --> 00:52:34.340
How did you get through it without laughing?
你是怎么忍住没笑场的？

1403
00:52:34.340 --> 00:52:38.740
How, your reaction when he says like a ham?
还有他那句“像火腿一样”，你的反应是怎么回事？

1404
00:52:38.900 --> 00:52:39.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1405
00:52:39.340 --> 00:52:41.660
And you're like, no, not exactly like a ham.
你当时那表情就像在说，不，没那么像火腿。

1406
00:52:42.020 --> 00:52:43.100
Jenna, it's so funny.
珍娜，这太搞笑了。

1407
00:52:43.220 --> 00:52:44.760
I don't even know how you kept a straight face though.
我真不知道你是怎么做到面不改色的。

1408
00:52:45.080 --> 00:52:51.100
My intention in that was like I was talking to like a five or a six-year-old and I couldn't
我当时的本意是，我就像在跟一个五六岁的孩子说话，我不能

1409
00:52:51.100 --> 00:52:55.780
let them see my real feelings about.
让他们看出我真实的感受。

1410
00:52:56.220 --> 00:52:57.400
The things they were saying.
关于他们说的那些话。

1411
00:52:57.420 --> 00:52:58.140
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1412
00:52:58.600 --> 00:53:01.040
We had a fan question from Susie Young, 22.
我们收到一个来自22岁的苏西·杨的粉丝提问。

1413
00:53:01.040 --> 00:53:04.620
She wanted to know if like a ham was scripted or improvised.
她想知道“像火腿一样”这句是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的。

1414
00:53:04.660 --> 00:53:05.820
It was improvised.
是即兴发挥的。

1415
00:53:06.000 --> 00:53:07.160
Did he improvise a bunch?
他即兴发挥了很多吗？

1416
00:53:07.400 --> 00:53:07.620
Yeah.
是的。

1417
00:53:07.880 --> 00:53:12.140
So on the day, we didn't really have an ending to this scene.
拍摄当天，我们其实还没想好这场戏怎么收尾。

1418
00:53:12.340 --> 00:53:12.620
Okay.
好吧。

1419
00:53:12.860 --> 00:53:17.400
We had him coming in and asking for advice and they wanted a button.
我们安排他进来寻求建议，然后他们想要一个结尾。

1420
00:53:17.620 --> 00:53:19.080
And this would often happen in scenes.
这种情况在拍戏时经常发生。

1421
00:53:19.280 --> 00:53:23.920
And the writers would then come over and give us a list of options.
编剧们就会过来给我们提供一堆选项。

1422
00:53:24.380 --> 00:53:24.430
Like suggestions.
就像建议一样。

1423
00:53:24.820 --> 00:53:25.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1424
00:53:25.740 --> 00:53:30.720
So like a ham was improvised, but then there were all these other options that were written
所以“像火腿一样”是即兴的，但纸上确实写了

1425
00:53:30.720 --> 00:53:31.500
on a piece of paper.
其他所有的选项。

1426
00:53:31.700 --> 00:53:38.080
And so we shot all of these things that he said, like, like a this, like a that, like
我们拍了他说的所有那些话，像这个，像那个，像

1427
00:53:38.080 --> 00:53:38.900
this, like that.
这个，像那个。

1428
00:53:39.000 --> 00:53:41.720
It was so hard not to laugh.
忍住不笑真的太难了。

1429
00:53:42.140 --> 00:53:45.600
I did laugh at like a ham because it wasn't on the piece of paper.
我确实在“像火腿一样”那句笑场了，因为那句没写在纸上。

1430
00:53:45.740 --> 00:53:47.040
So I was not expecting it.
所以我完全没预料到。

1431
00:53:47.040 --> 00:53:47.340
You didn't see it coming.
你没防备到他会这么说。

1432
00:53:47.340 --> 00:53:48.220
No, no.
没有，完全没有。

1433
00:53:48.220 --> 00:53:54.200
So that my response is definitely like take four or five because I remember everyone just
所以我那个反应镜头肯定是第四或第五次拍摄的，因为我记得他一说出口，大家就

1434
00:53:54.200 --> 00:53:55.480
lost it when he said it.
全都笑喷了。

1435
00:53:55.700 --> 00:53:57.840
And then they were like, okay, wait, that's good.
然后他们就说，好了，等等，那个不错。

1436
00:53:57.900 --> 00:53:58.260
That's good.
那个很好。

1437
00:53:58.320 --> 00:53:59.040
That's the one we want.
我们要的就是那个。

1438
00:53:59.160 --> 00:54:03.060
And so then they were like, pull it together and do it again.
然后他们就说，收敛一下，再来一遍。

1439
00:54:03.220 --> 00:54:03.720
Do it again.
再来一遍。

1440
00:54:03.860 --> 00:54:04.100
Okay.
好的。

1441
00:54:04.200 --> 00:54:05.140
I have a question for you.
我有个问题想问你。

1442
00:54:05.240 --> 00:54:07.540
When he says, shut up, I know exactly what to do.
当他说“闭嘴，我知道该怎么做”的时候。

1443
00:54:07.620 --> 00:54:08.600
Was that improvised?
那是即兴的吗？

1444
00:54:08.740 --> 00:54:09.820
That I don't remember.
那个我不记得了。

1445
00:54:10.040 --> 00:54:15.300
I don't remember because I do think that that final look to camera was, that was some direction
我不记得了，因为我觉得最后看向镜头的那个眼神，那是导演给的

1446
00:54:15.300 --> 00:54:19.220
I was given, which is like, I know the cameras out there.
指导，意思就是，我知道摄像机在那儿。

1447
00:54:19.400 --> 00:54:19.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1448
00:54:19.740 --> 00:54:22.220
And you're looking to cameras like, can this day get any worse?
你看向镜头时的表情就像在说，今天还能再糟糕点吗？

1449
00:54:22.360 --> 00:54:23.020
It's so weird.
太奇怪了。

1450
00:54:23.140 --> 00:54:24.300
I'm not getting any gifts.
我什么礼物都没收到。

1451
00:54:24.520 --> 00:54:24.640
No.
没有。

1452
00:54:24.980 --> 00:54:26.520
Jim has barely acknowledged me.
吉姆几乎没理我。

