《斯克兰顿的面孔》其实还有更多镜头。

1617
01:00:22.200 --> 01:00:25.740
Maybe that's the version that Michael submits to the film festivals.
也许那就是迈克尔提交给电影节的版本。

1618
01:00:26.060 --> 01:00:27.040
Well, but he tells.
嗯，但他说了。

1619
01:00:27.160 --> 01:00:28.020
So he's like, but you know what?
他当时就像是，但你知道吗？

1620
01:00:28.080 --> 01:00:29.180
Maybe it's not appropriate.
也许这不太合适。

1621
01:00:29.300 --> 01:00:29.680
Maybe not.
也许吧。

1622
01:00:29.680 --> 01:00:30.280
Maybe he will.
也许他会。

1623
01:00:30.360 --> 01:00:30.800
Maybe he won't.
也许他不会。

1624
01:00:30.800 --> 01:00:31.380
Maybe he won't.
也许他不会。

1625
01:00:31.420 --> 01:00:32.040
He's not sure.
他不确定。

1626
01:00:32.280 --> 01:00:33.680
The video doesn't go over well.
视频反响并不好。

1627
01:00:33.900 --> 01:00:34.460
They're stunned.
他们都惊呆了。

1628
01:00:34.600 --> 01:00:35.180
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1629
01:00:35.440 --> 01:00:38.800
Melora's reaction as Jan is just amazing.
梅洛拉饰演的简，反应简直绝了。

1630
01:00:39.000 --> 01:00:40.800
Melora, you crushed it.
梅洛拉，你演得太棒了。

1631
01:00:40.880 --> 01:00:41.520
I loved it.
我超喜欢。

1632
01:00:41.840 --> 01:00:44.280
So David just asks for his sales numbers.
所以大卫只是问了他的销售数据。

1633
01:00:44.500 --> 01:00:45.960
He's like, can I just get your sales numbers?
他就像是，我能只看你的销售数据吗？

1634
01:00:46.140 --> 01:00:48.860
And I was really worried for a second.
我当时有一瞬间真的很担心。

1635
01:00:49.080 --> 01:00:50.400
I was like, oh, no.
我心想，噢，不。

1636
01:00:50.600 --> 01:00:52.580
But no, Michael has those, too.
但并没有，迈克尔连那些都有。

1637
01:00:52.700 --> 01:00:54.300
He hands out some little binders.
他分发了一些小活页夹。

1638
01:00:54.420 --> 01:00:55.240
He was prepared.
他是有备而来的。

1639
01:00:55.360 --> 01:00:57.460
He had binders all ready to go.
他早就准备好了活页夹。

1640
01:00:58.200 --> 01:00:59.480
That's Michael in a nutshell.
这就是迈克尔的典型写照。

1641
01:00:59.480 --> 01:01:01.860
He's trying to be outside the box.
他试图跳出思维定式。

1642
01:01:02.060 --> 01:01:06.000
He's trying to tug on your heartstrings and make – this is his whole thing.
他试图触动你的心弦，让——这就是他的一贯作风。

1643
01:01:06.100 --> 01:01:09.660
He wants the work to be more than just a binder of numbers.
他希望工作不仅仅是一本数字活页夹。

1644
01:01:09.660 --> 01:01:11.400
He wants it to be about people.
他希望它能关乎人。

1645
01:01:11.640 --> 01:01:13.860
The thing is, they are his family.
问题是，他们就是他的家人。

1646
01:01:14.020 --> 01:01:14.320
Yes.
没错。

1647
01:01:14.320 --> 01:01:16.140
You know, things move at a slower pace.
你知道，事情进展得比较慢。

1648
01:01:16.320 --> 01:01:18.820
The song is with or without you.
那首歌是《With or Without You》。

1649
01:01:19.020 --> 01:01:21.240
It has nothing to do in the workplace.
它跟职场毫无关系。

1650
01:01:21.760 --> 01:01:21.940
No.
确实。

1651
01:01:22.020 --> 01:01:24.540
Like, what is – it's like a love song.
就像，这是什么——这就像是一首情歌。

1652
01:01:24.740 --> 01:01:24.980
Yeah.
没错。

1653
01:01:24.980 --> 01:01:31.120
And just when he was like, spend a day in Phyllis's pants, what does he say?
就在他说什么“在菲利斯的裤子里过一天”的时候，他到底说了什么？

1654
01:01:31.960 --> 01:01:34.640
Spend a day in Phyllis's pants is not what he says.
他说的根本不是“在菲利斯的裤子里过一天”。

1655
01:01:35.660 --> 01:01:38.400
Spend – oh, my God.
在——天哪。

1656
01:01:38.400 --> 01:01:43.420
Well, he says, like, see what it's like to walk a day in Oscar's shoes or –
好吧，他说的是，比如，看看像奥斯卡一样穿鞋过一天，或者——

1657
01:01:43.420 --> 01:01:44.740
Or sit in Phyllis's pants.
或者坐在菲利斯的裤子里。

1658
01:01:44.740 --> 01:01:46.240
I don't know what he says about Phyllis's pants.
我不知道他关于菲利斯的裤子说了什么。

1659
01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:48.680
It's right as she's sitting down in slow motion.
就在她慢动作坐下的时候。

1660
01:01:49.120 --> 01:01:50.000
I just love it.
我真是太喜欢了。

1661
01:01:50.400 --> 01:01:55.320
I hope this gave you a little taste of what life is like here at Dunder Mifflin Scranton.
希望这让你们稍微体会了一下邓德·米夫林斯克兰顿分公司的生活。

1662
01:01:55.620 --> 01:02:00.520
What it's like to walk a mile in Oscar's shoes or try on Phyllis's pants.
像奥斯卡一样穿鞋走一英里，或者试穿菲利斯的裤子。

1663
01:02:00.860 --> 01:02:01.640
There it is.
就是那句。

1664
01:02:01.840 --> 01:02:03.380
Or try on Phyllis's pants.
或者试穿菲利斯的裤子。

1665
01:02:03.380 --> 01:02:03.460
Okay, okay.
好了，好了。

1666
01:02:03.700 --> 01:02:06.400
So he says, try on Phyllis's pants.
所以他说的是，试穿菲利斯的裤子。

1667
01:02:06.420 --> 01:02:06.600
Yeah.
没错。

1668
01:02:06.880 --> 01:02:08.380
In slow-mo as she's sitting down.
在她坐下时的慢动作镜头里。

1669
01:02:08.540 --> 01:02:08.860
Yes.
是的。

1670
01:02:09.260 --> 01:02:10.240
Faces of Scranton.
斯克兰顿的面孔。

1671
01:02:10.420 --> 01:02:11.920
And then the very end, great Scott.
最后结尾那句，“天哪（Great Scott）”。

1672
01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:15.180
Mike said was – Mike sure said that was an afterthought.
迈克说的是——迈克确实说了那是后来才想到的。

1673
01:02:15.180 --> 01:02:17.960
But he just sort of added that last minute, and they made it.
但他只是临时加进去的，结果被剪进去了。

1674
01:02:18.080 --> 01:02:19.180
But it's so perfect.
但这太完美了。

1675
01:02:19.480 --> 01:02:20.540
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1676
01:02:20.940 --> 01:02:21.820
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1677
01:02:22.700 --> 01:02:23.340
All right.
好吧。

1678
01:02:23.500 --> 01:02:27.660
So now we're going to go back to the office again after that presentation.
现在在那场演讲之后，我们要回到办公室了。

