他说那是他妈妈送的。

1687
01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:40.240
And I loved his choice of putting the card in his pocket.
我很喜欢他把卡片放进兜里的那个选择。

1688
01:02:40.380 --> 01:02:40.820
Yeah.
没错。

1689
01:02:41.340 --> 01:02:42.440
He puts it in his pocket.
他把它放进了兜里。

1690
01:02:42.440 --> 01:02:43.500
Puts it in his pocket.
放进了兜里。

1691
01:02:43.500 --> 01:02:45.220
Meredith has passed out.
梅雷迪思晕过去了。

1692
01:02:45.380 --> 01:02:46.500
There's nothing for Pam.
帕姆什么都没有。

1693
01:02:46.640 --> 01:02:47.740
There's nothing for Angela.
安吉拉什么都没有。

1694
01:02:48.000 --> 01:02:48.200
Yeah.
没错。

1695
01:02:48.620 --> 01:02:51.160
And Meredith is going to sleep this one out.
而梅雷迪思打算睡过去。

1696
01:02:51.500 --> 01:02:53.140
Here's a fan catch.
这里有个粉丝发现的细节。

1697
01:02:53.620 --> 01:02:58.160
At 14 minutes, 45 seconds, Adam West, 84, says,
在14分45秒，84岁的亚当·韦斯特说，

1698
01:02:58.840 --> 01:03:02.720
there's a huge week calendar on the wall beside accounting
会计部旁边的墙上有一个巨大的周历，

1699
01:03:02.720 --> 01:03:06.460
that you can see from both accounting and from reception.
从会计部和前台都能看到。

1700
01:03:06.640 --> 01:03:07.920
It's always there.
它一直都在那儿。

1701
01:03:08.120 --> 01:03:08.560
It's always there.
它一直都在那儿。

1702
01:03:08.720 --> 01:03:10.580
It's a dry erase board calendar.
那是个白板日历。

1703
01:03:10.580 --> 01:03:11.200
Yes.
没错。

1704
01:03:11.460 --> 01:03:21.420
He said it has always bothered him that they abbreviate Thursday as T-H-U-S, thus, instead
他说他一直很介意他们把星期四缩写成T-H-U-S，也就是“因此”那个词，而不是

1705
01:03:21.420 --> 01:03:23.180
of T-H-U-R.
T-H-U-R。

1706
01:03:23.500 --> 01:03:26.520
And he said, quote, it breaks my mind.
他说，引用原话，这让他快疯了。

1707
01:03:26.920 --> 01:03:29.060
Well, I need to go back and see that.
好吧，我得回去看看。

1708
01:03:29.220 --> 01:03:30.860
14 minutes, 45 seconds.
14分45秒。

1709
01:03:31.220 --> 01:03:32.120
I mean, I know.
我是说，我知道。

1710
01:03:32.260 --> 01:03:34.280
I do remember the handwriting was a bit sloppy.
我确实记得那字迹有点潦草。

1711
01:03:34.280 --> 01:03:40.280
There is a chance that R looks like an S if it's in cursive.
如果那是连笔字的话，R看起来确实可能像S。

1712
01:03:40.420 --> 01:03:41.360
I'm going to go and look at it.
我要去看看。

1713
01:03:41.500 --> 01:03:42.200
I'm going to go check it.
我要去确认一下。

1714
01:03:42.340 --> 01:03:44.880
So you're thinking it's T-H-U-R?
所以你觉得应该是T-H-U-R？

1715
01:03:46.020 --> 01:03:46.660
You know what?
你知道吗？

1716
01:03:46.660 --> 01:03:47.320
I'll tell you what.
我跟你说吧。

1717
01:03:47.400 --> 01:03:48.660
It's not written in cursive.
那不是连笔字。

1718
01:03:48.780 --> 01:03:51.240
The days of the week are taped out.
星期几是用胶带贴出来的。

1719
01:03:51.400 --> 01:03:51.800
Oh.
噢。

1720
01:03:51.960 --> 01:03:53.000
In block letters.
是印刷体大写字母。

1721
01:03:53.140 --> 01:03:55.020
T-H-U-S, thus.
T-H-U-S，就是“因此”。

1722
01:03:55.400 --> 01:03:56.720
That would make me crazy, too.
那也会让我抓狂的。

1723
01:03:56.880 --> 01:03:57.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1724
01:03:57.220 --> 01:03:58.660
It's really bothering Adam.
这真的让亚当很困扰。

1725
01:03:58.680 --> 01:03:59.620
That's a crazy good catch.
这观察力真是绝了。

1726
01:03:59.620 --> 01:04:00.480
I'm going to go check it out.
我要去瞧瞧。

1727
01:04:00.480 --> 01:04:02.640
And I think it's just always that way.
而且我觉得它一直都是那样。

1728
01:04:02.820 --> 01:04:03.360
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1729
01:04:03.420 --> 01:04:04.580
I can't wait to go check it out.
我迫不及待想去看看了。

1730
01:04:05.000 --> 01:04:05.540
All right.
好吧。

1731
01:04:05.720 --> 01:04:09.300
So next, Jim's in the kitchen with Kelly.
接下来，吉姆在厨房和凯莉在一起。

1732
01:04:09.880 --> 01:04:14.720
And he is giving her, like, he is being a good friend, actually.
他正在给她建议，他其实表现得像个好朋友。

1733
01:04:14.720 --> 01:04:15.720
He's being gentle.
他很温柔。

1734
01:04:15.940 --> 01:04:17.300
And he's like, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1735
01:04:18.140 --> 01:04:19.360
He's just not into you.
他就是对你没意思。

1736
01:04:19.640 --> 01:04:21.560
