It's not what you give her.
重要的不是你送她什么。

1747
01:04:41.100 --> 01:04:43.080
It's that she knows you thought of her.
而是让她知道你心里有她。

1748
01:04:43.180 --> 01:04:43.460
Right.
对。

1749
01:04:43.460 --> 01:04:45.580
And that's desperately what Pam wants.
而那正是帕姆极度渴望的。

1750
01:04:45.680 --> 01:04:48.320
She just wants to feel like Roy thinks of her.
她只是想感觉到罗伊心里有她。

1751
01:04:48.360 --> 01:04:50.380
That he ever thinks of her.
感觉到他哪怕有那么一刻想到过她。

1752
01:04:50.620 --> 01:04:53.360
And then Jim is saying to Kelly, look,
然后吉姆对凯莉说，听着，

1753
01:04:53.480 --> 01:04:55.560
it'd be nice if he was into you, but he's not.
如果他喜欢你那当然好，但他不喜欢。

1754
01:04:56.000 --> 01:04:57.360
You just got to let it go.
你得学会放手。

1755
01:04:57.520 --> 01:05:00.020
And of course, Jim is talking about Pam.
当然，吉姆说的是帕姆。

1756
01:05:00.020 --> 01:05:00.460
Yes.
没错。

1757
01:05:01.040 --> 01:05:01.480
Yes.
是的。

1758
01:05:02.380 --> 01:05:04.640
And Kelly doesn't hear any of it.
而凯莉根本没听进去。

1759
01:05:04.640 --> 01:05:05.180
Kelly does not get it.
凯莉完全没明白。

1760
01:05:05.460 --> 01:05:08.000
She's like, you know, he invites her to poker.
她就像是，你知道，他邀请她去打扑克。

1761
01:05:08.140 --> 01:05:09.340
And she's like, can I invite Ryan?
然后她就问，我可以带瑞安一起去吗？

1762
01:05:09.560 --> 01:05:09.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1763
01:05:09.680 --> 01:05:12.960
And the face John does when she says that is like,
当她说完那话时，约翰的表情就像是，

1764
01:05:13.120 --> 01:05:14.160
come on.
拜托。

1765
01:05:14.180 --> 01:05:14.560
Come on.
拜托。

1766
01:05:14.640 --> 01:05:15.360
Come on.
拜托。

1767
01:05:16.700 --> 01:05:17.240
All right.
好吧。

1768
01:05:18.060 --> 01:05:19.520
So again, back to New York.
所以，回到纽约。

1769
01:05:19.660 --> 01:05:22.940
We go back and forth between New York and Scranton a lot in this episode.
这一集里我们一直在纽约和斯克兰顿之间来回切换。

1770
01:05:23.080 --> 01:05:27.320
This is when we find out that Craigers did not prepare anything for the meeting because
这时我们发现克雷格什么都没为会议准备，因为

1771
01:05:27.320 --> 01:05:28.920
he thought it was more of a meet and greet.
他以为这只是个见面会。

1772
01:05:28.920 --> 01:05:30.860
Well, he's also just a slacker.
嗯，他本来也就是个混日子的人。

1773
01:05:31.080 --> 01:05:32.060
He's a slacker.
他就是个懒鬼。

1774
01:05:32.440 --> 01:05:34.180
And he ignores direct orders.
而且他不服从直接命令。

1775
01:05:34.740 --> 01:05:36.880
I think his performance is so delicious.
我觉得他的表演真是太精彩了。

1776
01:05:37.540 --> 01:05:39.100
And he kind of gets in trouble.
然后他惹上麻烦了。

1777
01:05:39.260 --> 01:05:41.560
Jan says, this does not bode well for your branch.
简说，这对你们分部来说可不是什么好兆头。

1778
01:05:41.900 --> 01:05:43.880
And then he throws her under the bus.
然后他就把简给卖了。

1779
01:05:44.060 --> 01:05:44.300
Yeah.
没错。

1780
01:05:44.500 --> 01:05:45.360
He's like, what?
他就像是，什么？

1781
01:05:45.400 --> 01:05:48.800
I mean, I guess I'd get better treatment, you know, if we hooked up.
我的意思是，我想如果我和你有一腿，我大概能得到更好的待遇吧。

1782
01:05:48.940 --> 01:05:50.400
Like, that's what he's inferring, right?
他就是这个意思，对吧？

1783
01:05:50.480 --> 01:05:52.020
Because you hooked up with Michael.
因为你和迈克尔有一腿。

1784
01:05:52.020 --> 01:05:56.140
He flat out says, Michael made a stupid movie and didn't get in any trouble.
他直截了当地说，迈克尔拍了部烂片却没惹上任何麻烦。

1785
01:05:56.260 --> 01:05:57.860
Maybe I should have slept with you, too.
也许我也该和你睡一觉。

1786
01:05:58.140 --> 01:05:58.700
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1787
01:05:58.900 --> 01:05:59.320
Boom.
砰。

1788
01:05:59.780 --> 01:06:00.260
